[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3910533461","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116277#issuecomment-3910533461","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116277","id":3910533461,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7pFgFV","user":{"login":"mooflu","id":693717,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MzcxNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/693717?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu","html_url":"https://github.com/mooflu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-16T21:10:50Z","updated_at":"2026-02-16T21:10:50Z","body":"> As shown in the table above, table_h_separation/table_v_separation are used as padding for all cells in the table. They take effect simultaneously with custom padding in cells. Perhaps they should be used as margin?\r\n\r\nI think they should. Behaving more like a html/css table would be more familiar to most devs.\r\n\r\nI was looking into making table separations work consistently like margins. I.e. cell’s background color isn’t applied to it.\r\nMy still buggy WIP (yours covers both cell padding and table separations, so I’ll stop working on mine)\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/commit/e907b043c7317b14ac5e80b36c5906d546832a27\r\n\r\nPlayed around with your changes and it behaves much more consistent than before 🎉\r\nI did notice that horizontal cell padding can result in not matching the table box when text direction is set to right-to-left.\r\nAnd cell border not showing up all around the cell.\r\nRTL:\r\n<img width=\"238\" height=\"201\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d30072ad-b801-4ce0-a060-d2382ff1f83c\" />\r\n\r\nLTR:\r\n<img width=\"223\" height=\"199\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ac7020c5-3645-427b-9bef-e09db18499b8\" />\r\n\r\n```\r\n[table=3] \r\n[cell padding=0,0,0,0  bg=red][center]brown fox lazy dog[/center][/cell]\r\n[cell padding=10,0,0,0 bg=brown border=yellow][left]fox[/left][/cell]\r\n[cell padding=10,0,0,0 bg=darkgreen][right]dog[/right][/cell]\r\n[cell padding=10,0,0,0 bg=brown border=yellow][left]fox[/left][/cell]\r\n[cell padding=0,0,0,0  bg=red][center]brown fox lazy dog[/center][/cell]\r\n[cell padding=10,0,0,0 bg=darkgreen][right]dog[/right][/cell]\r\n[/table]\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3910533461/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3911434053","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116277#issuecomment-3911434053","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116277","id":3911434053,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7pI79F","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-17T01:40:36Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T02:55:33Z","body":"> I was looking into making table separations work consistently like margins. I.e. cell’s background color isn’t applied to it. \r\n\r\nDo you mean `cellspacing` in HTML?\r\n\r\n> I did notice that horizontal cell padding can result in not matching the table box when text direction is set to right-to-left.\r\n\r\nRegarding RTL, since the table is **inline**, and the `RichTextLabel` doesn't flip the other text horizontally after enabling RTL, I'm unsure at what step its Rect calculation reaches. Is its flip center the table center or the frame center?\r\n\r\nThis may need to be calculated along with other text.\r\n\r\nI'm not very familiar with RTL. Although some ancient Chinese books are read from right to left, they are actually read from top to bottom, then from right to left. This is different from RTL. \r\n\r\nSome ancient texts (calligraphy and painting) used as titles may appear to be RTL, but they can also be considered as one character per line. In short, this is not common in Chinese books.\r\n\r\n> I did notice that horizontal cell padding can result in not matching the table box when text direction is set to right-to-left.\r\n\r\nUnable to reproduce.\r\n\r\n> And cell border not showing up all around the cell.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1936744d-162e-452e-a370-04d77200fc78\r\n\r\nThe border not displaying may be due to floating-point precision.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3911434053/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3912166371","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116277#issuecomment-3912166371","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116277","id":3912166371,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7pLuvj","user":{"login":"mooflu","id":693717,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MzcxNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/693717?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu","html_url":"https://github.com/mooflu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-17T04:18:36Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T04:31:36Z","body":"> Do you mean `cellspacing` in HTML?\r\n\r\nyes, or `border-spacing` in css\r\n\r\n> The border not displaying may be due to floating-point precision.\r\n\r\nSorry if I wasn't clear. In RTL only using RichTextLabel's text direction. I would expect borders to show at 100% zoom like with LTR. Probably because of cell overlap in RTL.\r\n\r\nThis is what I see when I toggle RichTextLabel's text direction:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7708a820-a774-4463-a751-240eb1c03af3\r\n\r\n\r\njsfiddle to show rtl/ltr behavior for html/css. Click on the table to toggle ltr/rtl.\r\nhttps://jsfiddle.net/tue6m0rb/6/\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3912166371/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3912219270","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116277#issuecomment-3912219270","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116277","id":3912219270,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7pL7qG","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-17T04:33:58Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T05:07:06Z","body":"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8433bc84-7f22-40d5-9dec-63fe0a3f689b\r\n\r\nThe second table shows that it is **inline**. Furthermore, the other elements within the line are not sorted from right to left. This behavior is somewhat inconsistent. I'm not sure about its expected behavior either. \r\n\r\nIs it simply a matter of flipping the table layout horizontally in place? It seems that if other elements in the same row aren't flipped, this is the only option.\r\n\r\nThe Chinese character order isn't flipped, but the Chinese punctuation is. Confusing.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b5573278-dca1-41c9-abd0-b208d4a2f90f\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3912219270/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3912620216","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116277#issuecomment-3912620216","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116277","id":3912620216,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7pNdi4","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-17T06:43:53Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T06:45